<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  THE MULTI-SELECT BOX of a row — handoff README §7, «список приложений с
  чекбоксами», measured off the prototype's «Прокси по приложениям».

      22 × 22, radius 7, border 2dp
      снято  — заливки нет, обводка ?attr/colorOutline (#2A2E36)
      выбрано — заливка и обводка ?attr/colorPrimary

  A CHECKBOX AND NOT A SWITCH, and the difference is a promise, not a taste: a
  switch turns something on NOW, a checkbox marks a member of a set that some
  other control will act on. «Прокси по приложениям» is a set of 128 apps, so a
  column of switches down its right edge says 128 things are being turned on one
  at a time. The prototype draws boxes; this is that box.

  state_activated and not state_checked: the slot is an ImageView driven by
  RowBinder, not a CompoundButton, because the ROW owns the tap (the box is not
  separately focusable) and a Material checkbox would bring its own 48dp touch
  target and its own ripple back with it.

  Colours are ATTRIBUTES, never @color: the mono overlay redefines attributes and
  cannot reach a colour resource — the trap that left 22 tiles blue on a
  black-and-white screen.
-->
<selector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <item android:state_activated="true">
        <shape android:shape="rectangle">
            <solid android:color="?attr/colorPrimary" />
            <stroke
                android:width="@dimen/stroke_focus"
                android:color="?attr/colorPrimary" />
            <corners android:radius="@dimen/radius_checkbox" />
        </shape>
    </item>

    <item>
        <shape android:shape="rectangle">
            <solid android:color="@android:color/transparent" />
            <stroke
                android:width="@dimen/stroke_focus"
                android:color="?attr/colorOutline" />
            <corners android:radius="@dimen/radius_checkbox" />
        </shape>
    </item>
</selector>
